# sibling-slug-collision — case (b): two cross-lib code-is siblings whose names slugify identically.
library "Root".

// Root's decision `recommend`s an activity from EACH sibling (NO explicit
// `include`), so both enter the closure as SIBLINGS. "Sib One" and "Sib-One" both
// slugify to "sib-one", so Option B's disambiguator `<policyId>-sib-one` collapses
// them onto ONE local CodeSystem domain → the tailored sibling-slug-collision
// message + fail-closed.

concept "Trigger":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `trigger`.

decision "Route":
first:
- when "Trigger" then recommend activity "Sib One"."Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Sib-One"."Refer".
